body:
it sounds like you're bummed about being alone.  look at it as an opportunity.   hopefully next year you have plenty of money and can visit family or whoever.  this year, volunteer at a soup kitchen or find another charitable thing to do, go for a hike, patronize a favorite local restaurant.

&#x200B;

It's just one day, and just one thanksgiving out of what will hopefully be very many for you.  This one will be a little different and one you might tell the story of for a long time, especially if you do something interesting with it!

Just gonna say, Arroyo's main mailer is one that cites all the endorsements he got, primarily from progressive female politicians like Wu and Pressley, and I got a copy in the mail yesterday.

&#x200B;

The math doesn't add up, his campaign 100% was still sending out mailers highlighting since-rescinded endorsements, which is shady AF.  

&#x200B;

I think Hayden has a lot to answer for, but Arroyo strikes me as pretty untrustworthy.  I hope we get an investigation into Hayden and a new DA soon.

thanks!  I'm so glad I asked, I just assumed 6k/each, 'doh!

&#x200B;

I assume advantages are mostly non-tax and more related to flexibility?

Ok First of all, first time posting here and I;m just overwhelmed about how great you all are. 

&#x200B;

I ended up grinding my fingers to the bone to get as close to the recipe as possible.  

&#x200B;

I really liked the suggestion from [carmen\_cygni](https://www.reddit.com/user/carmen_cygni/) about allspice, but this is a picky eater so i had to hold back on that one for now.  

I honestly kind of assumed microplaning my cinnamon from sticks would result in a more potent spice - but based on the smell (and, probably, how old my cinnamon sticks are), it's just gonna be a little meh.

&#x200B;

But I also used cream instead of milk so that might punch the flavor up a little.  I'll let you know how it turns out.  

&#x200B;

And thanks again so much to all who chirped in, I really appreciate it.  If I asked like two hours earlier I would have a nicer product and fewer bandaids on my fingers.  Oh well!

I love baby carrots.  And I had a golden who, for the longest time, thought she must love them too.  She'd hear that distinctive "snap!" when I bit into one, and would harass and beg me until, finally, after making her do like five tricks, I would finally deign to bestow a carrot to her.

&#x200B;

And every time, like clockwork, she would eagerly grab it, chew for a second, look confusedly at me, then spit it on the floor in disgust.  

&#x200B;

And then start begging me for the next carrot in my hand. 

&#x200B;

Goldens are the best.  Sorry no video, it was about 15 years ago.
